# Memory Zones

# Zones are a single arena of memory
# this memory can be cleared in one operation
# zones can send data to each other, which implies mem.copy

# zones form a hierarchy of lifetime.  It is illegal to free a zone
# if any of it's children are still alive

# explicit threading operations must have their own zone.  We need to decide
# if these blocks have access to their ancestors' zone scope - maybe under
# certain conditions

